      "title": "US-bound flights out of Australia delayed after telecommunications outage grounded American planes",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/nov/14/us-bound-flights-out-of-australia-grounded-as-telecommunications-outage-affects-american-travel",
      "description": "<p>Sydney and Melbourne airports say flights were affected by now-lifted ban on departures in US</p><ul><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2026/nov/13/us-politics-latest-news-updates-democrats-republicans-donald-trump-van-hollen-chuck-schumer\">US flight outage – live updates</a></p></li><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">breaking news email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>Some US-bound flights from Sydney airport were grounded or delayed on Saturday after <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2026/nov/13/us-politics-latest-news-updates-democrats-republicans-donald-trump-van-hollen-chuck-schumer\">American authorities halted departures and delayed landings at all US airports</a>.</p><p>Flights from Melbourne airport were also affected, with travel for passengers expected to depart for Los Angeles shortly after 10am being delayed by almost three hours.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/nov/14/us-bound-flights-out-of-australia-grounded-as-telecommunications-outage-affects-american-travel\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-11-14T03:08:34"
    },
    {
      "title": "Stuart Bonds made ‘racist’ and ‘divisive’ comments. But One Nation is showing no sign of dumping the NSW candidate",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/nov/14/one-nation-nsw-candidate-stuart-bonds-ntwnfb",
      "description": "<p>The former coalminer’s claim Australians are being ‘demographically replaced’ sparked wide criticism, but his party has shown no signs of dumping him</p><ul><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">breaking news email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>In a Facebook video from a Sydney anti-immigration rally on Sunday, as a man dressed like a medieval knight watches on, One Nation’s lead upper house candidate, Stuart Bonds, launches into a speech against “mass” migration.</p><p>“Make no mistake, we are being demographically replaced inside our own nation,” he says.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/nov/14/one-nation-nsw-candidate-stuart-bonds-ntwnfb\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-11-14T01:00:30"
    },
    {
      "title": "Microsoft ‘deeply sorry’ for global disruption that could have billion-dollar impact on Australia",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/nov/14/microsoft-deeply-sorry-for-global-disruption-that-could-have-billion-dollar-impact-on-australia",
      "description": "<p>Experts say outage exposes ‘Australia’s reliance on foreign technology’ as software giant says services being restored</p><ul><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">breaking news email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>The <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2026/nov/13/microsoft-outage-outlook-teams-word-excel-reports\">Microsoft outage</a> could be a disaster for the Australian economy that forces some small businesses to close, with costs expected to run into the billions of dollars, experts have warned.</p><p>The US software company has said it is “deeply sorry” for a widespread outage that caused disruption to millions of users, organisations and businesses across the globe – and that it has “addressed the underlying issue”.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/nov/14/microsoft-deeply-sorry-for-global-disruption-that-could-have-billion-dollar-impact-on-australia\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-11-14T00:52:48"
    },
    {
      "title": "US aviation agency lifts nationwide ground stop affecting all air travel",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/nov/13/faa-nationwide-ground-stop-flights",
      "description": "<p>Sean Duffy, the transportation secretary, said the airspace was now open and the problem had been identified</p><ul><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2026/nov/13/us-politics-latest-news-updates-democrats-republicans-donald-trump-van-hollen-chuck-schumer\">FAA grounds thousands of flights – live</a></p></li></ul><p>The Federal Aviation Administration (FAA) has lifted a nationwide ground stop that was declared Friday afternoon, delaying or canceling more than 11,000 US flights, according to aviation tracker <a href=\"https://www.flightaware.com/live/cancelled/\">FlightAware</a>, and throwing airports into sudden chaos.</p><p>The FAA confirmed the airspace was open in an <a href=\"https://www.fly.faa.gov/adv/adv_otherdis?adv_date=11142026&amp;advn=5\">advisory on its website</a>. “So at 8.15 tonight, Eastern Time, we’ve opened up the airspace,” Sean Duffy, the US transportation secretary, said. “But it’s going to take us some time to unwind what’s happened this afternoon<em>.”</em></p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/nov/13/faa-nationwide-ground-stop-flights\">Continue reading...</a>",
